event: response.completed
data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":522,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_001eb130751901c3016adf27926e0081918062eb4cdb47c34b","object":"response","created_at":1793009554,"completed_at":1793009561,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You translate the supplied natural-language proof faithfully into Lean 4. Use the explicit project premises and any proved result in the pinned Mathlib environment. Preserve all assumptions, conclusions, equality modes and the supplied proof route. No reference answers, personal context, other tasks, shell or external services are available. Use the submit tool when the requested artifact is complete; if rejected, repair it. A strategy is advice, never an additional theorem or assumption. End this stage immediately when a submit tool reports stage_complete:true; the controller handles later stages. Within a proof stage, checked helper attempts are available through read_lean_draft. After a context reset, query its index before claiming no draft or helper exists. Helpers never become new premises. Use familiar interfaces directly; no background-note scan is required. For a relevant obstacle, select a matching local background_note_index entry and read_background_note if its details may help. Relate the actual Lean goal/context to its NL step: use the note grounds to identify a small missing application premise or transport, prove it from permitted inputs, then check the intended application. Verify actual types and conditions; a note is not a Lean proof or extra assumption. If it does not fit, continue ordinary allowed search or repair without insisting on that note or rebuilding a larger argument by default.","output":[{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_001eb130751901c3016adf2793a5108191850bf69be1b94965","call_id":"call_59587e22df8a4738bb645ca2e68f97ca","name":"submit_transition","arguments":"{\"proof\":\"intro x t ht\\nhave hopen : IsOpen (WM.dom n) := isOpen_lt continuous_const continuous_snd\\nhave hj : DifferentiableAt ℝ u (x,t) :=\\n  (h_H002.contDiffAt (hopen.mem_nhds ht)).differentiableAt (by simp)\\nhave hs : DifferentiableAt ℝ (fun r : ℝ => u (x,r)) t :=\\n  hj.comp t ((differentiableAt_const x).prodMk differentiableAt_id)\\nhave hd : HasDerivAt (fun r : ℝ => u (x,r)) (WM.ut u (x,t)) t := hs.hasDerivAt\\nlet f : ℝ → WM.Y m := fun r => if 0 < r then u (x,r) else q\\nhave heq : f =ᶠ[nhds t] (fun r => u (x,r)) := by\\n  filter_upwards [isOpen_Ioi.mem_nhds ht] with r hr\\n  have hr' : 0 < r := hr\\n  simp [f, hr']\\nhave hf : HasDerivAt f (WM.ut u (x,t)) t := hd.congr_of_eventuallyEq heq\\nhave hsq : HasDerivAt (fun r => inner ℝ (f r) (f r)) 0 t := by\\n  apply (hasDerivAt_const t (1 : ℝ)).congr_of_eventuallyEq\\n  filter_upwards [isOpen_Ioi.mem_nhds ht] with r hr\\n  have hr' : 0 < r := hr\\n  simp [f, hr', inner_self_eq_norm_sq_to_K, h_H004 x r hr']\\nhave hval : f t = u (x,t) := by simp [f, ht]\\nhave hh := (hf.inner ℝ hf).unique hsq\\nrw [hval, real_inner_comm (u (x,t)) (WM.ut u (x,t))] at hh\\nhave ho : inner ℝ (u (x,t)) (WM.ut u (x,t)) = 0 := by linarith\\nrefine ⟨ho, ?_⟩\\nobtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := h_H005 x t ht\\nrw [ha, inner_smul_right, real_inner_comm (u (x,t)) (WM.ut u (x,t)), ho, mul_zero]\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"Search the pinned mathlib Lean source using a regular expression; at most 100 lines.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"Read specified lines of a Mathlib/*.lean source file from the pinned checkout.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer